    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμο-πάτριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pr.</u>
			558
		</span></i>(lyr.) :—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>by
				the same father,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδελφεός</span> (
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φός</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.25
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				19.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				774e
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν ὁ. Ἡσιόναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδελφαὶ ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					11.2
